+
+<a id="compatibility"></a>
+## Compatibility
+
+Existing records omit the field and retain their previous pressure and billing behavior. The unchanged Session seed reader preserves the nested JSON in Assistant streams and finalized usage; older consumers ignore it for pressure and retain cumulative billing, so they keep their previous pressure behavior. New consumers use a supplied object only for pressure, use heuristic estimation and clear the prior occupancy sample for null, and use the legacy buckets when the field is absent. The optional field also appears in compaction/summary usage through the shared type, without changing that event's accounting or meaning. No model-visible content, replay authority, required event data, recovery rule, or Session writer version changes. Context-pressure checkpoints advance to state version 6 so their fold is rebuilt.
+
+<a id="verification"></a>
+## Verification
+
+pnpm exec vitest run packages/llm/token-meter/tests/token-meter.spec.ts packages/llm/token-meter/tests/token-usage-projection.spec.ts: 54 tests passed. Added cases serialize and restore omitted, null, and object samples through the existing Session seed reader, preserve both finalized and stream usage, retain cumulative billing, preserve header matching and the heuristic floor, and clear an unknown occupancy sample. The official persistence verifier classified all four additions across assistant/attempt, assistant/message, and compaction/summary as optional-property-added with no required compatibility review.
+
